From d6f5d34681dfc7d5436418aaf2f27d2b736fcec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BaptGosse <baptiste.gosselin@unxwares.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:38:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] chore(deps): update Go to 1.26.10 and vulnerable Go modules

Go 1.26.5 and several modules have known vulnerabilities that govulncheck reports as
reachable from Cloudreve:

- golang.org/x/net v0.55.0 (GO-2026-6603, GO-2026-6611, GO-2026-6612, GO-2026-6617)
- golang.org/x/text v0.37.0 (GO-2026-5970, GO-2026-6629)
- github.com/gorilla/websocket v1.5.0 (GO-2026-6278)
- github.com/ulikunitz/xz v0.5.12 (GO-2025-3922)

This moves the toolchain to go1.26.10, which fixes the standard library ones, and updates
these modules plus golang.org/x/crypto, golang.org/x/image, golang.org/x/mod and
github.com/klauspost/compress, which image scanners report with high severity fixes.
github.com/nwaples/rardecode/v2 stays at v2.1.0: v2.2.0 does not build with
github.com/mholt/archives v0.1.3.
---
 go.mod | 24 ++++++++++++------------
 go.sum | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++----------------------
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

